  "description": "CR 702.26b/702.26a Reality Ripple phases out a creature with no phasing, which phases back in at its own controller's next untap step",
  "note": "alice casts the Ripple on bob's turn, so her untap step (turn 2) comes before his (turn 3): it stays out through hers and is back at his, the schedule of the player it phased out under, which is bob who controls it, not the caster. The second Piker nobody aimed at is the falsifier for an effect that swept the board. The keyword decides who leaves, never who returns: having no phasing, it does not phase out again at once (turn 3) or at bob's next untap step (turn 5).",
